{"phase":211,"date":"2026-11-08","status":"FILING_LEVEL_PIT_CLOCK_FEASIBLE_PILOT_PANEL_NOT_ADMITTED","sample_design":{"source":"521 exact date-and-share Form 144/Form 4 links from Phase 210 exact-first graph","verified_pairs":5,"distinct_issuers":5,"selection":"five cross-issuer exact-link examples manually traced to SEC EDGAR filing-detail/header pages; not a representative panel audit","form144_snapshot":"2026 Q3 immutable Phase 69 artifact","form4_snapshot":"2026 Q3 immutable Phase 39 artifact"},"rules":{"event_semantics":"Form 144 is transmitted concurrently either with placing a broker sell order or with direct execution to a market maker. These are distinct event routes: broker-order placement may precede execution; direct market-maker filing may be contemporaneous with completed execution. The raw broker_or_market_maker field does not itself classify the route.","same_day_public_dissemination":"SEC EDGAR Filer Manual Volume II v74 explicitly lists Forms 3/3-A, 4/4-A, 5/5-A, 144 and 144/A as retaining the received-date filing date after 17:30 ET and being disseminated until 22:00 ET; the Form 144 guide also states same-day dissemination for accepted Form 144 submissions.","conservative_execution_clock":"Use the first regular-session open strictly after ACCEPTANCE-DATETIME. Do not use the acceptance second as an intraday fill timestamp because exact public-dissemination latency and execution venue are not established.","form4_role":"Form 4 is ex-post linkage/confirmation only; it is not a feature at the Form 144 event time.","non_execution_caveat":"A Form 144 does not prove completion. SEC staff says no amendment is required solely because the person does not sell the securities.","time_zone":"America/New_York (EDGAR Eastern Time); all sample timestamps below are EDT (UTC-04:00).","intermediary_classification":"Resolve the named intermediary to broker versus direct market-maker using an independent entity classification; quarantine ambiguous names. SEC Form 144